aec_eo_field_guide_read_offer,quests,Quest,,Read this field guide. It contains information only and has no objective or reward.
aecEOFieldGuideBook01,items,Item Name,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 1/10[-] | Progression & Game Stage
aecEOFieldGuideBook01Desc,items,Item Desc,,Read the AEC progression and Game Stage field guide.
aec_eo_field_guide_01_name,quests,Quest,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 1/10[-] | Progression & Game Stage
aec_eo_field_guide_01_text,quests,Quest,,"[FFD700]PROGRESSION & GAME STAGE[-] AEC difficulty follows your real Game Stage (GS), not only your character level. T00-T04 cover the pre-endgame grades: Basic, Feral, Radiated, Charged and Infernal. The full endgame route begins at GS 600 with T05 Veteran, then advances through T06 Brutal, T07 Savage, T08 Ravager, T09 Dread, T10 Nightmare, T11 Apex, T12 Overlord, T13 Titan, T14 Cataclysm and T15 Mythic. Higher tiers increase health, damage, speed, mobility and rewards. Check the AEC skill-tree tab for your current GS thresholds. Quests can force a precise tier inside their active POI; outside quests, wilderness selection remains dynamic."
aecEOFieldGuideBook02,items,Item Name,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 2/10[-] | Newbie Protection
aecEOFieldGuideBook02Desc,items,Item Desc,,Read how AEC protects players below GS 100 and GS 600.
aec_eo_field_guide_02_name,quests,Quest,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 2/10[-] | Newbie Protection
aec_eo_field_guide_02_text,quests,Quest,,"[50DC50]NEWBIE PROTECTION[-] At GS 0-99, full newbie protection is active: dangerous AEC events do not directly target you, their nearby-spawn effects are blocked for you, and Heatmap or Storm Hazard boosts are ignored by your surrounding wilderness spawns. Kills may still be recorded by the world systems, but you are not selected as their dangerous target. At GS 100-599, the absolute newbie shield has ended, yet the AEC T05+ wilderness tier route is still locked: boosted Game Stage from Heatmap or Storm cannot promote your normal wilderness spawns into the GS 600 endgame ladder. Heat can still build and Hazard can still rise for the biome, but Heatmap bosses and Nemesis appearances require an eligible player at GS 600 or higher."
aecEOFieldGuideBook03,items,Item Name,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 3/10[-] | Heatmap Pressure
aecEOFieldGuideBook03Desc,items,Item Desc,,"Read the current Heatmap gain, decay, warning and cooldown rules."
aec_eo_field_guide_03_name,quests,Quest,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 3/10[-] | Heatmap Pressure
aec_eo_field_guide_03_text,quests,Quest,,"[64B4FF]HEATMAP PRESSURE[-] The active system tracks combat pressure by biome. Every eligible zombie kill adds 1% Heat. After 60 real seconds without a kill, Heat decays by 5% per real minute. Players are warned at 70%; reaching 100% primes the next escalation. The 64-metre cell setting is used for local density and follower-overcrowding checks, not as the scope of the biome-wide Hazard level. Nearby feedback appears through Safe Zone, Heat and Hazard HUD buffs. A completed escalation chain has a 60-minute restart cooldown. Heatmap boss events remain separate from Blood Moon logic. Staying and fighting keeps pressure high; leaving combat quiet allows it to cool."
aecEOFieldGuideBook04,items,Item Name,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 4/10[-] | Hazard 0-5
aecEOFieldGuideBook04Desc,items,Item Desc,,Read how Heatmap escalation changes biome danger from Hazard 0 to 5.
aec_eo_field_guide_04_name,quests,Quest,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 4/10[-] | Hazard 0-5
aec_eo_field_guide_04_text,quests,Quest,,"[FF8800]HAZARD ESCALATION[-] Hazard 0 means Heat is building but no biome tier boost is active. Each successful 100% Heat cycle raises the biome by one Hazard level and can arm a boss with 4 escorts. At GS 100-599, Heat and Hazard may accumulate, but the boosted-GS wilderness route is blocked and no protected low-GS player is chosen as the boss target. From GS 600 onward, that block is removed: repeated Heat cycles can keep increasing the biome without another GS gate, one level at a time, up to the hard limit Hazard 5. Each Hazard step can promote ordinary wilderness spawns above their normal GS tier. When Heat reaches zero and the biome remains quiet for at least five minutes, Hazard can fall one level. Hazard 5 is maximum pressure: relocate, cool the biome or fortify."
aecEOFieldGuideBook05,items,Item Name,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 5/10[-] | Dynamic Spawning
aecEOFieldGuideBook05Desc,items,Item Desc,,"Read how wilderness, POI, biome, Storm and Blood Moon spawning differ."
aec_eo_field_guide_05_name,quests,Quest,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 5/10[-] | Dynamic Spawning
aec_eo_field_guide_05_text,quests,Quest,,"[FFD700]DYNAMIC SPAWNING[-] The AEC controller enhances vanilla spawning instead of replacing it blindly. It evaluates context, real GS, biome and day or night, then chooses an eligible weighted tier and family. Wilderness encounters may form leader-and-follower packs; followers can be weaker than their leader. Current safeguards suppress custom pressure within 100 metres of a Land Claim Block and stop follower injection when the local 3x3 cell neighborhood exceeds 15 zombies. Pine Forest remains the T05-T15 safe biome. During an active AEC quest, tier override applies only to the active POI clear phases; the outside world remains dynamic. Storm spawning is enabled in the shipped settings and adds one tier step where valid. Blood Moon uses separate scaling and boss rules."
aecEOFieldGuideBook06,items,Item Name,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 6/10[-] | AI World Events
aecEOFieldGuideBook06Desc,items,Item Desc,,Read how biome invasions and the AI Master event schedule work.
aec_eo_field_guide_06_name,quests,Quest,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 6/10[-] | AI World Events
aec_eo_field_guide_06_text,quests,Quest,,"[FFCC33]AI WORLD EVENTS[-] The AI Master schedules world pressure with a random 60-120 real-minute delay between selections. Events can target a biome, run for a limited window and sometimes migrate when they end. Active families include Doomlord, Singerie, Druid, night-only Ghost, Mushroom, Headless and Archer invasions, plus Mega-Horde, Heatmap increase or decrease, Ghost-on-kill pressure and boss incursions. The shipped rules disable Kill Replacement and multiplied-airdrop events by assigning them zero weight. Event and Nemesis clocks pause while no living player is connected; their deadlines shift when players return, preventing an instant backlog. GS 0-99 players are not dangerous-event targets. Treat server messages and HUD warnings as operational intelligence, not decoration."
aecEOFieldGuideBook07,items,Item Name,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 7/10[-] | Nemesis Roster
aecEOFieldGuideBook07Desc,items,Item Desc,,"Read about persistent Nemesis identities, ranks, progression and death."
aec_eo_field_guide_07_name,quests,Quest,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 7/10[-] | Nemesis Roster
aec_eo_field_guide_07_text,quests,Quest,,"[FF3333]NEMESIS ROSTER[-] Nemesis are persistent world-level AEC enemies, not disposable random bosses. Each record stores a unique name, title, rank, linked family and tier, home territory, combat history and virtual health, attack, defense and speed. Six ranks form the hierarchy: Lesser, Greater, Elite, Champion, Legendary and World. Victories, defeats and simulation conflicts can change their standing over time. Death is not always permanent: each Nemesis rolls its own permanent-removal threshold between 2 and 5 deaths, and death or despawn starts a respawn cooldown. Empty roster slots are refilled under population rules rather than instantly. Their state is saved to JSON, so identities, ranks, territories, grudges and death history survive world reloads."
aecEOFieldGuideBook08,items,Item Name,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 8/10[-] | Nemesis Wars
aecEOFieldGuideBook08Desc,items,Item Desc,,"Read about Nemesis grudges, revenge, territory wars and migration."
aec_eo_field_guide_08_name,quests,Quest,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 8/10[-] | Nemesis Wars
aec_eo_field_guide_08_text,quests,Quest,,"[FF8800]GRUDGES, WARS & MIGRATION[-] Defeating a Nemesis can create a personal grudge; killing a related ordinary AEC boss can also provoke family vengeance. Revenge checks are timed and pair-cooldown protected, while recently respawned players receive anti-chain protection. Nemesis can fight one another in power struggles and scheduled territory wars. Related allies may intervene and add simulation boosts; winners can rise, losers can fall, and titles may change with rank. Territory wars continue to resolve in the world, but players below GS 600 cannot trigger a Nemesis appearance by entering a territory or war zone. Nemesis can migrate their home coordinates over long intervals, so an old safe route may later cross a hostile domain. Names, titles and rank-colored HUD auras identify the threat when one is nearby."
aecEOFieldGuideBook09,items,Item Name,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 9/10[-] | Contracts & Tokens
aecEOFieldGuideBook09Desc,items,Item Desc,,"Read how trader contracts, POI sizes, tier overrides and tokens work."
aec_eo_field_guide_09_name,quests,Quest,,[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 9/10[-] | Contracts & Tokens
aec_eo_field_guide_09_text,quests,Quest,,"[5599FF]CONTRACTS & TOKENS[-] Trader AEC contracts combine an enemy tier T00-T15 with a POI size A1-A5. Activate the rally point, clear the sleepers, remain inside the POI and return to a trader. During clear phases, the listed AEC tier is forced only inside that POI. Completion awards universal AEC Tokens and tier-scaled rewards; higher tiers and larger objectives award more Tokens. Trader availability follows trader tier and game stage.\n\nThe 419-step AEC EO campaign covers Minion and Boss families from 0★ through 5★, including Research Papers, passive sample miners and the final T15 A5 challenge. The Contract Relay provides a renewable daily list of Boss and Minion contracts and can resummon its drone after a chunk unload."
aecEOFieldGuideBook10,items,Item Name,,"[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 10/10[-] | Samples, Market & Gear"
aecEOFieldGuideBook10Desc,items,Item Desc,,Read the AEC crafting economy from kill rewards to endgame mutators.
aec_eo_field_guide_10_name,quests,Quest,,"[66B3FF]AEC FIELD GUIDE 10/10[-] | Samples, Market & Gear"
aec_eo_field_guide_10_text,quests,Quest,,"[D9B36C]SAMPLES, MARKET & GEAR[-] Credited AEC kills award tiered mutation samples and Infected Teeth directly to the player. Completed AEC contracts award universal AEC Tokens. Use the Mutation Exchange to upgrade five samples into one sample of the next tier, or downgrade one sample into five of the previous tier.\n\nThe Zombie Market Terminal is the economy hub: request a Crypto Miner, power it with the correct battery, install family and star Connection Cards, produce boss coins, then invest those coins in Research Papers, Passive Part Miners, contracts and supplies. The AEC Extreme Workstation and Necroforge use universal Tokens and tiered mutation samples for endgame modifiers and equipment. Blood Moon ranking rewards remain personal, while Heatmap boss events are handled separately."
